boundary='Only the required C1-LOG-UNAVOIDABLE source claim is supported by this new proof package. BODY review accepted with explicit delta; integrated root/Tests/harness, shared registry/site/pixels, FINAL review, native acceptance and PR remain separate gates. Chapter1 remains open:16 source items, mandatory proof total unknown(null), full regret/minimum, NoRegret and six existing main-relative contributor gaps remain required. Chapter2 is incomplete; Chapters3–16 are unenumerated and necessary appendix dependencies remain required. Total Goal ACTIVE. Exact stacked OPEN unmerged PR190 base9425fecb38be60b1acb7a918cb149f72117133ad; no main/live/merge/deployment claim.'
source_delta='Orabona v10 printed p.4/PDF p.16 states that logarithmic dependence is unavoidable and explicitly gives no minimax-optimality proof there. H(T+1)/6 and log(T+2)/6 are derived quantitative support, neither printed nor claimed sharp. This is not a numbered source theorem.'
model='Histories h are newest-first binary lists. K(h) counts true labels; q(h)=(K(h)+1)/(|h|+2), w([])=1 and w(b::h)=w(h)*(q(h) if b=true else1-q(h)). This same normalized positive binary law depends on neither learner policy nor seed. Normalization and nonnegativity are proved before constructing the shared finite-action probability measure and integral. The chronological stream is reverse(h); padding beyond its length is never used by regret. The prediction at Lean round t receives reverse of the chronological strict prefix of length t. The current label is revealed after prediction. Source round1 is Lean0.'
assumptions='For every measurable seed space Ω, every probability measure μ, every policy A:Ω→List Bool→ℝ with each history section ω↦A(ω,h) measurable and A(ω,h)∈[0,1] for every seed and every history, and every positive natural horizon T, the terminal produces ONE binary vector v of length T outside the seed integral. The seed may encode the full private random tape; each policy remains strict-past. The integral is genuinely integrable: actual signed path regret has absolute value at most T, proved from bounded squared losses, and measurable history sections yield measurable finite loss sums. No Bochner nonintegrability fallback or assumed regret certificate is used.'
parameters='H_n=Σ_{i=1}^n1/i and log is natural log; squared loss is (x-y)^2 without1/2. Labels0/1 are legal source [0,1] outcomes and learner outputs are real [0,1]. The deterministic intermediate expected-regret bound allows arbitrary real history outputs. The probability law/count moments are total at T0, q([])=1/2, but all lower terminals require T≥1. Regret is signed cumulative regret, never average regret, clipped regret or absolute regret. The exact shifts are H(T+1) and log(T+2).'
proof='Actual recursive normalization gives E_T[K]=T/2 and E_T[K²]=T(2T+1)/6, hence E_T[q(1-q)]=(T+3)/(6(T+2)). Causal prefix identities generate the actual same-path cumulative learner-loss successor. Conditional square loss is at least q(1-q), so summing its actual expected increments gives learner loss at least T/6+(H(T+1)-1)/6. The shared empirical mean is proved feasible and globally minimizes the same binary path square loss; its produced expected optimum is (T-1)/6. Subtracting these same-path quantities proves E_T[R_A]≥H(T+1)/6 for any real strict-history policy. For bounded measurable seed policies, proved integrability permits finite weighted sum/integral interchange. Strictly positive normalized path weights imply some ONE path has seed-average regret at least H(T+1)/6. Mathlib log_add_one_le_harmonic gives the log endpoint. These are actual compiled proof dependencies, separate from the curated teaching route.'
exclusions='The witness may depend on the algorithm family, its seed law and T, but never on the realized seed. There is no almost-sure, high-probability, every-seed, uniform-seed or single-infinite-sequence assertion; no sharp minimax coefficient or representation theorem for every possible randomized oracle.'
validation='Sixteen named canaries compile actual causality, dependent two-step weights1/3 and1/6, T0/T2 normalization, first/second count moments1 and5/3, variance5/24, actual same-path regret13/36 and optimum1/2, the one-step1/4 lower endpoint, deterministic Dirac specialization and a genuinely two-atom seed policy with different outputs0/1 and atom masses1/2. The seeded T2 harmonic endpoint is11/36. Numerical/type identity checks are validation, not substitutes for universal theorem bodies. Seventy-six named kernel checks use only standard Lean axioms;64 actual closed proposition and12 definition identities compile, with recursive/nominal equality bridges where rfl is insufficient. Thirty specified compiler VALUE pairs are checked; this is not a teaching-edge inventory.'
math=r'\begin{aligned}q(h)&=\frac{K(h)+1}{|h|+2},\quad w([])=1,\\w(b::h)&=w(h)\,[bq(h)+(1-b)(1-q(h))],\\x_t(A_\omega,v)&=A_\omega([v_{t-1},\ldots,v_0]),\quad\bar v=T^{-1}\sum_{t<T}v_t,\\R_{A_\omega}(v)&=\sum_{t<T}(x_t-v_t)^2-\sum_{t<T}(\bar v-v_t)^2,\\\forall(\Omega,\mu)&:\ \mu(\Omega)=1,\quad\forall A:\Omega\to\operatorname{List}(\{0,1\})\to\mathbb R,\\[\forall h:&\ \omega\mapsto A_\omega(h)\ \text{measurable}],\quad[\forall\omega,h:\ A_\omega(h)\in[0,1]],\\\forall T\ge1\quad&\exists v\in\{0,1\}^{T}:\\\frac{\log(T+2)}6&\le\frac{H_{T+1}}6\le\int_\Omega R_{A_\omega}(v)\,d\mu(\omega).\end{aligned}'
